  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories. I can't see their code from here. ARCH-4 says changes to the event must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. \"Nothing reads it\" would need confirming against those two consumers. Even then, deleting the field in one step could break a deployed consumer that still parses it.\n\nThe event and the model are also tied together. `src/core/events.ts:50` builds the event from `order.channel`, so removing it from the model forces it out of the event.\n\nThere are two ways forward:\n\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).** In this change I would:\n   - Stop requiring `channel` on `POST /orders`, so the validation and the request parsing no longer fail without it.\n   - Remove it from the `Order` model.\n   - Keep `channel` on `OrderPlaced`, marked `@deprecated`, with a fixed placeholder value. Consumers then still get the field.\n   - Remove the field from the event later, once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it.\n\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** I'd do this if you can confirm both consumer teams have already stopped reading `channel` and that the removal is approved. I would remove it from the event, the model, validation, request parsing, the tests and the docs.\n\nWhich do you want? If you pick option 2, tell me the consumers are confirmed.",
